Right now, a billion people are chronically hungry.

235
00:23:35,980 --> 00:23:41,000
That means they wake up hungry, they're hungry all day, and they go to sleep hungry.

236
00:23:41,560 --> 00:23:43,700
A billion people are living in slums.

237
00:23:44,260 --> 00:23:47,640
Not the same billion people, but there is some overlap.

238
00:23:48,560 --> 00:23:52,940
Living in slums means they don't have infrastructure to take the garbage away.

239
00:23:53,380 --> 00:23:56,160
They don't have secure water supplies to drink.

240
00:23:57,740 --> 00:24:00,040
Nearly a billion people are illiterate.

241
00:24:00,040 --> 00:24:03,300
Try to imagine your life being illiterate.

242
00:24:03,960 --> 00:24:08,340
You can't read the labels on the bottles in the supermarket if you can get to a

243
00:24:08,340 --> 00:24:14,220
supermarket. Two -thirds of those people who are illiterate are women, and about 200

244
00:24:14,220 --> 00:24:20,120
to 215 million women don't have access to birth control they want so that they can

245
00:24:20,120 --> 00:24:21,680
control their own fertility.

246
00:24:22,760 --> 00:24:25,220
This is not only a problem in developing countries.

247
00:24:25,960 --> 00:24:29,200
About half of all pregnancies globally are unintended.

248
00:24:29,200 --> 00:24:33,140
So those are examples of population problems.

249
00:24:34,420 --> 00:24:38,620
Demography gives you the tools to understand and to address these problems.

250
00:24:39,060 --> 00:24:43,540
It's not only the study of human population, but the populations of non -human

251
00:24:43,540 --> 00:24:50,140
species, including viruses like influenza, the bacteria in your gut, plants that you

252
00:24:50,140 --> 00:24:53,800
eat, animals that you enjoy, or that provide you with meat.

253
00:24:53,800 --> 00:24:59,920
Demography also includes the study of non -living objects like light bulbs and taxi

254
00:24:59,920 --> 00:25:03,240
cabs and buildings because these are also populations.

255
00:25:04,120 --> 00:25:09,180
It studies these populations in the past, present, and future using quantitative

256
00:25:09,180 --> 00:25:13,040
data and mathematical models as tools of analysis.

257
00:25:14,280 --> 00:25:18,300
I see demography as a central subject related to economics.

258
00:25:18,300 --> 00:25:24,120
It is the means to intervene more wisely and more effectively in the real world, to

259
00:25:24,120 --> 00:25:29,280
improve the well -being not only of yourself, important as that may be, but of

260
00:25:29,280 --> 00:25:33,320
people around you and of other species with whom we share the planet.

